From 5c3e3774c32c778d845001fa743c3e072b587367 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ali Asiri <assiri@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 17:52:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] i18n(web): complete the Arabic locale
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The dashboard has its own Arabic catalogue, separate from the desktop one, and
it had the same silent-fallback problem: `ar` is the only web locale that goes
through `defineLocale`, so anything it omitted rendered in English without a
type error or a failing test.

It supplied 574 of 714 English strings — 140 rendering in English (80.4%). This
translates all of them, bringing `web/src/i18n/ar.ts` to 100%.

Largest gaps closed: cron scheduling (32), profiles (32), kanban (21), sessions
(17), custom env keys (10).

Notes for review:

- Purely additive: 146 insertions, no deletions. No previously translated string
  is touched.
- Placeholders (`{count}`, `{name}`, `{time}`, `{n}`, `{days}`, `{column}`) are
  preserved exactly, and `scheduleModes.weekdaysShort` keeps its seven entries.
- `env.customConfigured` drops the `{s}` token deliberately. Call sites do
  `.replace("{s}", n !== 1 ? "s" : "")`, which appends a Latin "s" — meaningless
  in Arabic. Omitting the token makes the replace a no-op and the string reads
  correctly.
- Terminology follows the catalogue's existing choices (البوابة، الملف الشخصي،
  الجلسة، المهارات)، with product and protocol names left in Latin script.

This makes Arabic the most complete locale in the dashboard: every other locale
is a `Translations` literal and each is missing the same 79 optional keys.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
